From af571218d8b96ccc5c1659458e8c01f9b73d7572 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: builder <builder@localhost>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 19:29:22 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] sepolicy: quiet SystemUI's lookup of the Bluetooth app's data
 dir

SystemUI draws the Bluetooth app's notifications (its file transfer
summaries are re-posted at every boot) with that app's resources;
creating the class loader makes the linker resolve the bundled app's
library permitted paths, which include /data/user_de/0/
com.android.bluetooth (bluetooth_data_file): two getattr denials per
boot. SystemUI loads no code from there, so keep it denied, quietly.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 sepolicy/platform_app.te | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 sepolicy/platform_app.te

diff --git a/sepolicy/platform_app.te b/sepolicy/platform_app.te
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..26c8b0e
--- /dev/null
+++ b/sepolicy/platform_app.te
@@ -0,0 +1,6 @@
+# SystemUI draws the Bluetooth app's notifications (file transfer summaries, which it re-posts at
+# every boot, pairing requests) with that app's resources. Creating the app's class loader makes
+# the linker resolve its library permitted paths, which for a bundled app include its data
+# directory (/data/user_de/0/com.android.bluetooth, bluetooth_data_file). SystemUI loads no code
+# from there: keep the lookup denied, quietly.
+dontaudit platform_app bluetooth_data_file:dir getattr;
-- 
